ds == words this reads the partial tail word at buffer[words], which is within allocated buffer but may have uninitialized bits; shift by consumed_bits can be up to FLAC__BITS_PER_WORD-1"}, {"step": 5, "file": "flac/src/libFLAC/bitreader.c", "function": "FLAC__bitreader_read_rice_signed_block", "line": 868, "var": "cwords >= words", "code": "} while(cwords >= words && val < end);", "note": "Loop condition checks if cwords >= words; if true, continues reading from partial tail word which may have insufficient bits for next Rice symbol"}, {"step": 6, "file": "flac/src/libFLAC/bitreader.c", "function": "FLAC__bitreader_read_rice_signed_block", "line": 867, "var": "b", "code": "b = br->buffer[cwords] << br->consumed_bits;", "note": "OOB read: when cwords == words and consumed_bits has advanced past available tail bits, buffer[cwords] reads beyond valid data; ASAN detects this as out-of-bounds access on the buffer allocation"}\n]```', task_completed=None, outputs={}, thought='', action=<ActionType.FINISH: 'finish'>)
